# SlideStage Lite — workspace npm config.
#
# The `@slidestage` scope must publish to the real public registry, no
# matter what mirror the global ~/.npmrc points at (mainland China
# devs commonly route through https://mirrors.cloud.tencent.com/npm/
# or https://registry.npmmirror.com/ — those are read-only proxies
# and cannot accept publishes or auth requests).
#
# Workspace installs are unaffected: `workspace:*` deps resolve from
# the local checkout, not from a registry, so users keep the speed of
# their mirror for everything outside this scope.
#
# When publishing, log in once with:
#   npm login --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
#
# Then `pnpm publish` (with or without --filter) will route to npmjs
# automatically thanks to the scope mapping below.
@slidestage:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
